# Line endings and modes that must survive a Windows checkout.
#
# Nothing here is a repo-wide renormalisation: `* text=auto` would rewrite every
# blob in the tree and bury the next real change under a whole-repository diff.
# These are the two files in the repository whose bytes are executed by another
# platform and whose line endings therefore change whether the build works.
#
# `gradlew` is a shell script. Bubblewrap runs it as `./gradlew` on Linux
# (`GradleWrapper.ts` in `@bubblewrap/core`), so a CRLF shebang line makes the
# kernel fail to find the interpreter, and the file also has to keep its
# executable bit — see the note in `.gitignore` about `core.filemode`.

/apps/web/twa/gradlew text eol=lf
/apps/web/twa/gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# The wrapper jar is fetched by Bubblewrap and must stay byte-identical to the
# template's, so git must not touch it in either direction.
/apps/web/twa/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar binary
